(Rolling Element Bearing Diagnostics: Envelope Demodulation and Spectral Analysis) Tj T*
(Section 1: Physical Mechanism of Localised Bearing Defects) Tj T*
(When a rolling element strikes a localised spall on the inner or outer raceway, it) Tj T*
(produces a short-duration broadband impulse that excites structural resonances of) Tj T*
(the bearing assembly and transducer mounting \(commonly 2000 to 6000 Hz\).) Tj T*
(Because rolling elements experience random slip of 1 to 2 percent under load,) Tj T*
(high-order harmonics in the direct baseband FFT smear out, whereas demodulating) Tj T*
(a band-pass filtered resonance band via the Hilbert transform \(envelope spectrum\)) Tj T*
(extracts the repetition rate \(BPFO, BPFI, BSF, FTF\) with high signal-to-noise ratio.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
