(Section 2: Why a Single FFT Peak Does Not Confirm a Bearing Fault) Tj T*
(An isolated peak in the raw FFT spectrum near a theoretical bearing characteristic) Tj T*
(frequency \(FTF, BPFO, BPFI, or BSF\) is never definitive proof of a bearing defect.) Tj T*
(Coincidental peaks frequently arise from electrical line harmonics \(50/60 Hz and) Tj T*
(multiples\), gear-mesh or belt pass tones, blade/vane pass frequencies, or shaft) Tj T*
(harmonic distortion from misalignment and mechanical looseness.) Tj T*
(Diagnostic confirmation requires corroborating evidence across multiple indicators:) Tj T*
(\(1\) harmonic series \(1x, 2x, 3x\) in the high-frequency envelope spectrum,) Tj T*
(\(2\) modulation sidebands \(1x shaft RPM sidebands around BPFI; FTF sidebands around BSF\),) Tj T*
(and \(3\) elevated impulsiveness in time-domain kurtosis \(> 4.0\) and crest factor \(> 5.0\).) Tj T*
ET
endstream
