(Section 3: Time-Frequency Spectrogram and Additional Recommended Measurements) Tj T*
(Short-Time Fourier Transform \(STFT\) spectrograms reveal whether high-frequency) Tj T*
(energy occurs as periodic transient vertical stripes \(characteristic of impacts\)) Tj T*
(or continuous stationary horizontal bands \(characteristic of tonal noise or) Tj T*
(continuous rubbing\).) Tj T*
(When vibration analysis indicates a potential raceway or rolling-element defect,) Tj T*
(recommended follow-up measurements include: tri-axial accelerometer measurements) Tj T*
(\(horizontal, vertical, axial\), high-frequency envelope trending, phase measurement) Tj T*
(across couplings to rule out misalignment, infrared thermography of the bearing) Tj T*
(housing, and oil/grease ferrography for metallic spall particles.) Tj T*
ET
